# Cloudflare Pages cache-control overrides.
#
# Hashed build assets (assets/index-<hash>.js, fonts, etc.) keep Pages' default
# long-lived immutable caching — their content can't change without a new name.
#
# The PWA entry points, though, MUST always be revalidated so a new deploy takes
# effect immediately instead of being masked by a stale cache:
#   - sw.js / registerSW.js — the service worker. If the browser serves a stale
#     sw.js, it never detects the new version, so the precached (old) app shell
#     keeps being served forever. `no-cache` forces a revalidate every load, so
#     `registerType: 'autoUpdate'` can pick up the new SW and reload to it.
#   - / and index.html — the unhashed entry document.
#   - manifest.webmanifest — referenced by the entry document.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/registerSW.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
